    "lawCode": "Amd §224-d, Lab L",
    "lawSection": "Labor Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4881\n\nSPONSOR: SCARCELLA-SPANTON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the labor law, in relation to requiring contractors and\nsubcontractors performing construction work for covered renewable energy\nsystems to use apprenticeship agreements\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThis bill would extend the current apprenticeship requirements already\nin law for thermal energy networks to all covered renewable energy\nsystems.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\n§ 1- Amends subdivision 8 of section 224-d of the Labor Law, as added by\nChapter 375 of the Laws of 2022, to require all contractors and subcon-\ntractors performing construction work of renewable energy systems over 1\nMW or larger receiving renewable energy credits, thermal energy\nnetworks, offshore wind supply chain projects receiving New York State\nEnergy Research and Development Authority (NYSERDA) funding, and major\nutility transmission facilities to use apprenticeship agreements with\npre-apprenticeship direct entry providers registered with the Department\nof Labor.\n\n§ 2 - Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nA highly trained and skilled workforce is needed in the clean energy\nsector to realize the ambitious goals of the Climate Leadership and\nCommunity Protection Act (CLCPA). As the shift toward renewable energy\nsources progresses, it is imperative that workers are trained in the New\nYork State Department of Labor (NYSDOL) certified apprenticeship\nprograms to ensure the state's workforce is prepared and equipped to\nbuild the state's clean energy future. Apprenticeship requirements on\nrenewable energy projects will ensure workers are adequately trained to\nbuild clean energy infrastructure in a skilled, safe, timely and effi-\ncient manner. Additionally, apprenticeship requirements provide local\nworkers with opportunities to gain access to career-track jobs, changing\nlives and bolstering local economies.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
