    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4881A\n\nSPONSOR: SCARCELLA-SPANTON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the labor law, in relation to requiring contractors and\nsubcontractors performing construction work for covered renewable energy\nsystems to use apprenticeship agreements\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThis bill would extend the apprenticeship agreement requirements already\nin law for thermal energy networks to all covered renewable energy\nsystems.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\n§ 1 - Amends subdivision 8 of section 224-d of the Labor Law, as added\nby Chapter 375 of the Laws of 2022, to require all contractors and\nsubcontractors performing construction work of renewable energy systems\nover 1 MW or larger receiving renewable energy credits, offshore wind\nsupply chain projects receiving New York State Energy Research and\nDevelopment Authority (NYSERDA) funding, and major utility transmission\nfacilities to use apprenticeship agreements.\n\n§ 2 - Effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION:\n\nRemove pre-apprenticeship direct entry programs registered with the\nDepartment of Labor as a requirement for covered renewable energy\nsystems besides thermal energy networks.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nA highly trained and skilled workforce is needed in the clean energy\nsector to realize the ambitious goals of the Climate Leadership and\nCommunity Protection Act (CLCPA). As the shift toward renewable energy\nsources progresses, it is imperative that workers are trained in New\nYork State apprenticeship programs to ensure the state's workforce is\nprepared and equipped to build the state's clean energy future. Appren-\nticeship requirements on renewable energy projects will ensure workers\nare adequately trained to build clean energy infrastructure in a\nskilled, safe, timely and efficient manner.  Additionally, apprentice-\nship requirements provide local workers with opportunities to gain\naccess to career-track jobs, changing lives and bolstering local econo-\nmies.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
